:: Ending: The Rope [ending] {"position":"1400,1080","size":"100,100"}
<span class="stub"><span class="beat"><b>ENDING 4 — THE ROPE.</b> Fagin's last night in the condemned cell at Newgate, and Oliver is brought to see him. Fagin will not say where the papers are and does not know who Oliver is any more.</span><span class="note">Structural: the coldest ending. Reached by testifying against Fagin (whatever else the run earned), or by refusing with a run that fell short of the Locket. Oliver survives, gets nothing back, and watches the only person who ever wanted him hang.</span><span class="note">Splits on `$gaveUpFagin`: if the player testified, the visit to the cell is something Oliver asked for and regrets; if not, Brownlow brings him. Also worth a `$nancySaved` grace note — one thing saved out of all of it.</span></span>

